==================================================
 Actaria Engine Documentation
==================================================

Actaria SDL is an Entity Definition Language (EDL)
used to describe game scenes, triggers, characters
and other gameplay entities.

--------------------------------------------------
 Actaria Engine Pipeline
--------------------------------------------------

1) Compiler reads entity definitions from plain
   text EDL files.

2) Actaria Linker validates global and local
   symbol usages.

3) Oriented Story Graph (OSG) linker validates:
   * Connectivity (game completeness)
   * Existence of leaves (game endings)
   * Reachability of a leaf from any node
     (game finiteness)

4) All validated entities are serialized into a
   hex-formatted bytecode file executable by the
   Actaria Virtual Machine.

--------------------------------------------------
 Actaria Virtual Machine
--------------------------------------------------

The Virtual Machine executes the game according
to the following algorithm:

while (!endOfGame) {
    while (!endOfDialog) {
        handlePlayerReaction();
        // dialog context update
    }
    handleDialogVerdict();
    // scene and game context update
}

--------------------------------------------------
 Oriented Story Graph Requirements
--------------------------------------------------

* Connectivity
* Existence of leaves
* Reachability of a leaf from any node

--------------------------------------------------
 Virtual Machine Bytecode Format
--------------------------------------------------

    <version><s>{<section>}[,...s]<root_scene_id>

* version        — bytecode format version
* s              — number of sections
* root_scene_id — starting scene identifier

--------------------------------------------------
 Section Format
--------------------------------------------------

    <section> ::= <entity_type><n>{<entity>}[,...n]

* entity_type
  FNV-1a hash of the entity type name.

* n
  Number of entities in the section.

* entity
  Binary representation of an entity.

--------------------------------------------------
 Entity Type Identification
--------------------------------------------------

* Hash algorithm: FNV-1a
* Hash is generated at compile time
* Hash collisions are undefined behavior
  and must be prevented by the compiler

--------------------------------------------------
 Notes
--------------------------------------------------

* Entities are grouped by type into sections.
* Section order is not significant.
* All mandatory fields are fixed-size (2–4 bytes).
* After game termination, the hex dump
  is no longer updated.

